1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:15,400
-crf 0: lossless in libaom, not in libsvtav1.

2
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:26,500
Measured on ffmpeg 6.1.1 and 8.1.2.

3
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:32,800
Five questions about AV1 encoding.

4
00:00:32,800 --> 00:00:41,630
Each answer is measured on two builds.

5
00:00:41,630 --> 00:00:49,940
Reader 1: ffprobe and ffmpeg filters.

6
00:00:49,940 --> 00:01:01,030
Reader 2: our own byte walk and PSNR.

7
00:01:01,030 --> 00:01:11,170
-crf 30: SVT 61 kB, libaom 41 kB (6.1.1).

8
00:01:11,170 --> 00:01:21,320
On 8.1.2 SVT is 82 kB, libaom 41 kB.

9
00:01:21,320 --> 00:01:30,640
libaom -crf 0 is lossless.

10
00:01:30,640 --> 00:01:41,830
SSIM 1, PSNR infinite, frames equal.

11
00:01:41,830 --> 00:01:57,920
SVT -crf 0 = no -crf. Its log says CRF 35.

12
00:01:57,920 --> 00:02:03,770
Lossy on both builds.

13
00:02:03,770 --> 00:02:12,200
-crf 64: out of range, no file.

14
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:20,640
-crf 63 works: 6 kB, SSIM 0.94.

15
00:02:20,640 --> 00:02:27,910
-b:v 0 next to -crf: nothing changes.

16
00:02:27,910 --> 00:02:34,140
Identical packets, both encoders, both builds.

17
00:02:34,140 --> 00:02:48,310
6.1.1, SVT 1.7: the bitrate is ignored.

18
00:02:48,310 --> 00:03:02,490
8.1.2, SVT 4.1: an error, no file.

19
00:03:02,490 --> 00:03:11,460
libaom obeys -b:v next to -crf.

20
00:03:11,460 --> 00:03:23,410
Noisy clip: 512 kB down to 223 kB.

21
00:03:23,410 --> 00:03:35,130
SVT preset 12 is 55% bigger than 8.

22
00:03:35,130 --> 00:03:45,390
And looks worse: SSIM 0.99 vs 0.997.

23
00:03:45,390 --> 00:03:54,380
Noise: preset 12 is bigger, no better.

24
00:03:54,380 --> 00:04:05,930
6.1.1: 622 vs 730 kB. 8.1.2: 708 vs 747.

25
00:04:05,930 --> 00:04:16,020
SVT: keyframes at 0, 161, 322.

26
00:04:16,020 --> 00:04:29,480
libaom: frame 0 only. -g 25: 16 each.

27
00:04:29,480 --> 00:04:40,080
Frame 300: SVT runs 140 frames.

28
00:04:40,080 --> 00:04:50,680
libaom 301. With -g 25: 1.

29
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:59,750
-g 25 costs libaom 18% (6.1.1), 19% (8.1.2).

30
00:04:59,750 --> 00:05:07,680
SVT: 1% on 6.1.1, 5% on 8.1.2.

31
00:05:07,680 --> 00:05:17,800
Check -crf 0, -b:v, preset, -g.

32
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:24,550
Measure, do not assume.

33
00:05:24,550 --> 00:05:34,670
Measured on ffmpeg 6.1.1 and 8.1.2.

34
00:05:34,670 --> 00:05:46,490
Not tested: real footage, players, other builds.
